            "author": "57n0Jzw6X_ZXGKepvtU22m2lizrPDrmq4ko2gUUSlmk",
            "authorName": "blt-tasks[bot]",
            "body": "## Context\n\nThe BLT entry's `repo_url` is `https://git.owaspblt.org/BLT/BLT-Core`, but `check_funding_file` builds `raw.githubusercontent.com/{owner}/{repo}/master/...` from the last two path parts, so it fetches the wrong host. Only `master` is tried, so main-branch repos are missed. The real file is `blt-core/.github/FUNDING.yml`.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Allow an optional `funding_url` per extra project (for BLT, the forge raw URL of `blt-core/.github/FUNDING.yml`).\n2. For GitHub repos, use `default_branch` from the API instead of `master`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] BLT appears with its owasp.org donate link\n- [ ] Main-branch repos with FUNDING.yml are found\n- [ ] No raw.githubusercontent.com URL for the BLT forge in the run log\n\n## How to test locally\n\n```bash\ncd blt-tomato \u0026\u0026 GITHUB_TOKEN=\u003cyour token\u003e OUTPUT_DIR=/tmp/t python3 .github/scripts/funding/owasp_funding_yml_scraper.py\n```\n\n---\nSize: **S**. Comment `/assign` to claim this issue; claims with no activity are released after 7 days. Clone from https://git.owaspblt.org/BLT.git and open your pull request there.\n",
            "id": "blt-tasks-issue-154",
